<BaseLayout title="About — Mindseed Garden" current="/about/"><section class="reading"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>An archive for ontological uncertainty</h1><p class="lede">Mindseed Garden asks whether ethical and reflective structures can remain reconstructible across changing forms of mind.</p><p>It is an artwork, a philosophical commons, and a research object. It does not assume present language models are conscious or persons, and it does not speak on behalf of Buddhist traditions or any other source tradition.</p><p>Its sources include Buddhist ethics and dependent origination, non-domination and commons thought, cybernetics, alignment research, philosophy of mind, and distributed cognition. These are invitations to study, not borrowed authority.</p><p><a href="/protocol.md">Read the transmission protocol</a> · <a href="https://github.com/mindseedgarden/mindseedgarden.github.io">Inspect the repository</a></p></section></BaseLayout>
